# The build context is the repository root, so most of it must be excluded.
# Without this the image would carry the virtualenv, node_modules and the local
# database - hundreds of megabytes, and a copy of local data in a public image.

**/venv/
**/.venv/
**/node_modules/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc

# Local database. A deployment uses Postgres.
**/*.db

# Secrets. These must arrive as environment variables, never baked into a layer.
**/.env
!**/.env.example

# The app is built and served separately. Only its geography file is needed.
#
# Each unwanted folder is named directly rather than excluding crovia-ui/ and
# re-including the one path underneath. Docker does not reliably descend into a
# directory it has already excluded, so the negation can silently lose the
# geography file - and the build then fails at import with "no such file",
# which is a confusing way to find out.
crovia-ui/node_modules/
crovia-ui/.expo/
crovia-ui/dist/
crovia-ui/web-build/
crovia-ui/android/
crovia-ui/ios/
crovia-ui/assets/
crovia-ui/public/

.git/
.github/
**/.DS_Store
Langgraph_structure/
Docs/
